    <Citation_Information>
      <author_list>Thomas, P.C.</author_list>
      <publication_year>2021</publication_year>
      <description>Image mosaic of 243 Ida.  This image mosaic is a high-pass filtered version
constructed from Galileo SSI images in a simple cylindrical projection.  The images
used were those at and after FDS 202558300 on a low-pass filtered map of the lower
resolution images. Black areas are those with unprojectable surfaces.  Resolution on
original images varied greatly, so some regions of low intrinsic resolution are very
oversampled in the resampled mosaic.  The highest resolution on the images used to
create the mosaic is approximately 25 m/pixel.  The scale is 7 pixels/degree.  The
mosaic is centered on 0 latitude, 0 longitude, with longitude increasing to the east.
 See Thomas, et al. (1996) for description of mosaic contents.</description>
